        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "ac2dd53d-42cf-52ea-b2f1-455d62660be6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Martin Degville, Richie Furay, Stephen Stills, Neil Young, Bruce Palmer, Dewey Martin, Jim Messina, Rusty Young, George Grantham, Randy Meisner, Rusty Egan, Steve Strange, Boy George, Marilyn, Alice Temple, Perri Lister, Princess Julia, Philip Sallon, Carl Teper, Tony James\n- Bands: Sigue Sigue Sputnik, Buffalo Springfield, Poco\n- Places: Walsall\n- Songs: Love Missile F1-11\n- Organizations: EMI, Rock & Roll Hall of Fame\n\nFacts:\n- Richie Furay was born on May 9, 1944.\n- Martin Degville was born on 27 January 1961 in Walsall.\n- Richie Furay is an American singer, songwriter, and Rock & Roll Hall of Fame member.\n- Richie Furay helped form Buffalo Springfield with Stephen Stills, Neil Young, Bruce Palmer, and Dewey Martin.\n- Richie Furay helped form Poco with Jim Messina, Rusty Young, George Grantham, and Randy Meisner.\n- In 1986, Sigue Sigue Sputnik had a worldwide hit single with \"Love Missile F1-11.\"\n- Martin Degville is the lead singer and co-songwriter of the UK pop band Sigue Sigue Sputnik.\n- Sigue Sigue Sputnik had six other single releases on EMI.\n- Martin Degville later became the frontman of Tony James' Sigue Sigue Sputnik.\n- Attendees mentioned in relation to the Blitz Kids scene included Rusty Egan, Steve Strange, Boy George, Marilyn, Alice Temple, Perri Lister, Princess Julia, Philip Sallon, Carl Teper, and Martin Degville.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
